    {
      "number": 9,
      "id": "PR_kwDON--yp86PSrno",
      "title": "Sketch signature-based retry configs",
      "url": "https://github.com/grittygrease/draft-sullivan-tls-implicit-ech/pull/9",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "dennisjackson",
      "authorAssociation": "NONE",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "This PR sketches a design where the retry_configs are authenticated via a signature rather than via the TLS certificate. \r\n\r\nThis avoids connection failures when the server can't distinguish between GREASE and a client with a stale ECHConfig.",
      "createdAt": "2025-03-19T14:44:03Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-07-23T09:47:40Z",
      "baseRepository": "grittygrease/draft-sullivan-tls-implicit-ech",
      "baseRefName": "main",
      "baseRefOid": "07cbd99d7646a7dd696efa9b925b90c8435b9e9f",
      "headRepository": "dennisjackson/draft-sullivan-tls-implicit-ech",
      "headRefName": "simple-signing",
      "headRefOid": "bbfa9711f3c62cbafbe7ff876a442435ab143017",
      "closedAt": null,
      "mergedAt": null,
      "mergedBy": null,
      "mergeCommit": null,
      "comments": [],
      "reviews": [
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDON--yp86hdkgF",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "500d148"
          },
          "author": "martinthomson",
          "authorAssociation": "NONE",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:23:40Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 35,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n      opaque retry_signing_key_hash<1..255>;\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:23:40Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 34,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n      SignatureScheme signature_algorithm_id; // Defined in RFC 8446 4.2.3\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:25:01Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 61,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n      SignatureScheme signature_algorithm_id; // Defined in RFC 8446 4.2.3\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:25:10Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 40,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n      RetryKey retry_keys<1..255>;\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:25:28Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 33,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n      HashAlgorithm hash_algorithm_id; // Needs a new IANA registry\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe number of hash algorithm registries that IANA maintains is potentially worth another XKCD 927-style joke.\r\n\r\nThankfully, we have https://www.iana.org/assignments/tls-parameters/tls-parameters.xhtml#tls-parameters-18 which can be revived.",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:26:23Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 62,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n      HashAlgorithm hash_algorithm_id; // Needs a new IANA registry\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:26:31Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 81,
              "body": "Could this be a new message type, like NewSessionTicket, with the ECH extension only signaling that a new config will be provided?",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T00:35:50Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 107,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\nIf ECH is accepted, then the same procedure as-in {{I-D.ietf-tls-esni}} is followed.\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T01:30:22Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 117,
              "body": "It is not 100% clear that this refers to the extension that the client received via other means (either a DNS SVCB lookup or a previous retry config.  There's a potential for this to be mistaken to refer to the value in the retry config, which would not work.",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T01:33:29Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 121,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\nas specified in {{I-D.ietf-tls-esni, Section 6.1.6}} without considering the server's TLS certificate.\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T01:33:55Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 188,
              "body": "It looks like the procedures you define won't allow this to be propagated without causing ECH failures.  At least in the transition from public_name to key hashes.\r\n\r\nIt wasn't obvious to me that the text on Enterprise policy was intended to encompass the existing public_name-based retry method.  If that is the case, then this probably needs to be clearer.",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T01:38:04Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 196,
              "body": "I'd extend this a fair bit longer than 48 hours.  The value of the thing being protected here is far less than what a certificate protects and those last for longer.",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T01:39:33Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 209,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\n{{I-D.ietf-tls-esni}} specifies how retry_configs are authenticated based on the public_name specified\r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-03-24T01:39:55Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-03-24T01:40:39Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDON--yp861ls4-",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "500d148"
          },
          "author": "dennisjackson",
          "authorAssociation": "NONE",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2025-07-23T09:47:40Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-07-23T09:47:40Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 188,
              "body": "It's not explicit in the draft, but I think servers can support traditional ECH and implicit ECH simultaneously. Clients that don't know about Implicit will ignore the extension (and work fine). ",
              "createdAt": "2025-07-23T09:47:40Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-07-23T09:47:40Z"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
